# raw emulator captures (the published webp files are committed; these are not)
img/_raw/

# The generators are LOAD-BEARING and must not be ignored.
#
# `_*` above was ignoring every one of them, so the site's walking pace, its stride constant, its
# length-drift check and the photo-credit builder existed ONLY on one machine. A fresh clone would
# have regenerated the site with the old, wrong pace and nobody would have known. That is the same
# failure as the auto-commit that reported "pushed" for months while pushing nothing: work that
# exists but is nowhere.
#
# Checked before un-ignoring: none of them carry a credential. This repo is PUBLIC.
!_gen_profiles.py
!_gen_attribution.py
!_gen_satmaps.py
!_gen_trailmaps.py
!_shots_to_web.py
!_sync_trail_colors.py
# 2026-07-17. The allowlist above un-ignored the six generators but MISSED THE MODULE THEY IMPORT.
# `_trail_colors.py` -- the ONE source of truth for trail colour, the fix for the four-hand-copied-
# palettes drift -- starts with an underscore, so `_*` ate it and it was never pushed. PROVEN, not
# assumed: `git archive origin/main | tar -x` into a temp dir, then `python -c "import _gen_satmaps"`
# -> ModuleNotFoundError: No module named '_trail_colors'. Every generator on the remote was dead on
# arrival, which is the exact "work that exists but is nowhere" failure described above -- fixed for
# the callers and left live for the dependency. An allowlist has to cover the import graph, not the
# entry points.
# `_gen_polarmap.py` builds the South Pole card (mercator is undefined at the poles) and was ignored
# the same way. `_gen_route_overlay.py` draws the route as vector over the basemap; without it
# `_gen_trailmaps.py` cannot build a card.
# Checked before un-ignoring, same as above: none of the three carries a credential. This repo is PUBLIC.
!_trail_colors.py
!_gen_polarmap.py
!_gen_route_overlay.py
